{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"reasonless-defunct-earwig","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe checked-in complexity ratchet (.github/complexity-baseline.json) records several moderate-CCN functions in the pure, well-tested `graph` blocker subsystem: _blockers.py::_find_direct_blockers (CCN 18), _graph.py::check_cycle_at_level (16), _graph.py::_get_all_blocked_by (20), _unblock.py::detect_newly_unblocked (22). These are LOW-RISK (well below the 30-45 high-risk orchestrators, which are deliberately out of scope), pure-logic, already type-clean (graph is in the mypy strictness ratchet), and have ZERO in-progress file_impact contention.\n\n## Plan\n- Extract clear sub-steps (e.g. traversal helpers, predicate builders) to lower branching without changing observed graph results.\n- Lean on the existing graph unit/interface tests as the behavioral oracle; add cases only if a seam is newly exposed.\n- Lower the shrink-only complexity baseline entries accordingly (never raise).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The four named functions have reduced CCN with graph outputs unchanged.\n- [ ] .github/complexity-baseline.json entries for these functions are equal or lower (shrink-only).\n- [ ] Complexity, type, lint, and full test gates green.\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches src/rebar/graph/_blockers.py, _graph.py, _unblock.py and the shrink-only baseline entries — all free of in-progress contention.","id":"985c-32d2-e828-4e6a","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","priority":3,"tags":["remediation","complexity","ae1b"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Reduce cyclomatic complexity of the graph blocker subsystem (CCN 16-22, low-risk)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786